#Program 0
The return type of function f is int, representing the result of the operation. If the results overflow the range of int, then return -1

### Example Output:

```
2
```

### Samples:
## [java](/cpp)
```c++
#include <cstdio>
#include <vector>

using namespace std;

int f(int N, vector<pair<string, long long>> members, int M, vector<string> changes)
{
    long long ans = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        int flag = 0;
        for (int j = 0; j < changes.size(); j++) {
            string op = changes[j];
            int type = (op[0] == '+')? 1 : -1;
            string name = (type == 1)? op.substr(3) : op.substr(2);
            if (name == members[i].first) {
                ans += members[i].second * type;
                flag = 1;
                break;
            }
        }
        if (flag == 0) {
            ans += members[i].second;
        }
    }

    return ans;
}
```

